From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MyNaai Dev <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Bulk product upload: template, dry run, one transaction per row, undo

The admin panel can now add dozens of products at once: download a sample sheet,
fill it in, upload it, read a per-row report, and undo the import if it was a
mistake.

  GET  /api/shop-products/bulk/template?format=xlsx|csv   admin — the file itself
  POST /api/shop-products/bulk/import                     admin, multipart/form-data
                                                          file, mode, dryRun
  POST /api/shop-products/bulk/undo                       admin, { importId }

The template is generated from the importer's OWN column list
(`shopProductBulk.service.COLUMNS`), so "the headers in the sample" and "what the
import accepts" cannot drift. It has three sheets: Products (header row, frozen,
filtered, with a comment on every column), Example (two filled rows — a separate
sheet so they can never be imported by accident) and Instructions (the rules in
customer language, including the photo spec: square 1200×1200 JPG, white
background, ≤250 KB).

Columns: productName*, category*, gender, price*, mrp, description, rating,
isAvailable, stockCount, imageUrl1…4, barCode, hsnCode, gstPercent.
(* = required. Headers are matched by NAME after stripping punctuation, so
"Product Name" and "product_name" both work and a deleted column is reported by
name instead of shifting every value one cell left.)

Rules the code enforces:

  · ONE TRANSACTION PER ROW, not per file. A bad row is reported and skipped; the
    other 117 products still land. An all-or-nothing import would let one typo in
    row 400 destroy an evening's work.
  · `dryRun: true` validates everything and writes nothing (no products, no audit
    row) — the panel always calls it first and quotes the numbers back.
  · `CREATE_ONLY` reports an existing name as SKIPPED (never FAILED);
    `UPSERT` updates it in place. Match is case-insensitive per catalogue, and a
    name repeated inside one sheet is refused with "Duplicate of row N".
  · the report's `row` is the SPREADSHEET row number, not an array index, so the
    admin can find it in Excel. Every message names the column and the fix:
    `"₹499" is not a number — put the price in as digits only`,
    `Unknown category "hair oil" — use one of the ids from the template`,
    `The MRP (300) is lower than the price (500) — swap them or leave the MRP blank`.
  · refusals of the WHOLE file name the limit hit: 415 for a non-spreadsheet,
    413 for over 5 MB, a 400 naming the missing header column, and a 400 for more
    than 1000 rows.
  · each created row carries `bulk_import_id`; `bulk/undo` soft-deletes exactly
    those. A product the sheet only UPDATED keeps no handle, so undo can never
    delete something an admin created by hand.
  · the audit row (`shop_product_imports`) records the admin, the file name, the
    mode, the counts and the non-successful rows, plus `undone_at` when undone.

Files

  new  src/services/shopProductBulk.service.js       columns, template, parser,
                                                     validation, import, undo
  new  src/utils/middleware/bulkUpload.middleware.js multer in memory, 5 MB,
                                                     xlsx/csv only, friendly errors
  new  src/controller/shopProduct/downloadBulkTemplate.js
  new  src/controller/shopProduct/bulkImportShopProducts.js
  new  src/controller/shopProduct/undoBulkImport.js
  new  src/database/models/shopProductImport.model.js
  mod  src/database/models/shopProduct.model.js      bulk_import_id, stock_count,
                                                     bar_code, hsn_code, gst_percent
  mod  src/routes/shopProduct.routes.js              the three routes
  mod  package.json / package-lock.json              + exceljs ^4.4.0

The migration in backend-1 adds `shop_product_imports`, `shop_products.bulk_import_id`
and the four optional product columns; `ensureShopSchema` re-creates them idempotently.

Apply after backend-1-shop-categories (uses `ensureShopSchema` and
`shopCategoryService.resolveCategoryId`). Then `npm install` on the server so
exceljs is present — `npm ci` works too, the lockfile is in this patch.

Verified: the template was generated and read back (three sheets, 16 headers in
order, ExcelJS opens it); a filled .xlsx and a quoted .csv were parsed with the
right sheet row numbers; a 1001-row sheet, a missing header column and a .pdf are
each refused with the limit named; and the import loop was run against a stub
ORM — dry run writes nothing, 2 good rows land while rows 4 and 5 are reported,
CREATE_ONLY skips existing names, UPSERT updates without creating, undo removes
exactly the created rows and leaves an updated one alone, and a second undo is
refused.
